~ start
Alithia Undersen: You’re right, mister Asker. This is an answer only I can give to myself. 
Alithia Undersen: We’ve... lost too many. Our very goals have been shattered. 
Alithia Undersen: This is the end. The messengers have already found the truth. 
Alithia Undersen: And I’ll be the one to finish it after all has been done. Holding the truth, only I can uphold the final act to my standards. 
Alithia Undersen: Everyone is gathered around the small village. I walk on the village center, up the elevated platform that exists there. 
prometheus: “I cannot refute any of these...” 
Alithia Undersen: Everyone’s attention is slowly drawn onto me. 
enfina: “I just want you all to be okay...” 
Alithia Undersen: I raise my hand as some of the monks start getting wary and discussing if they should take me off the stage. 
Cyrus Rowe: “You are so very petty, do you know that?” 
Alithia Undersen: I release my other hand. The wooden platform responds with several thuds as it rolls onto it before stopping. The only object that can bring an ending to all of this. 
Alithia Undersen: The die is cast. 
=> END